# AGENTS.md: how to work in this repository

This file is for any AI coding agent (and any human). It is tool-neutral on purpose.
Project: **<%title%>**: <%description%>

## The one rule
**"Done" means `./scripts/sdlc verify` exits 0 and you can show its report.** Not "the code looks right", not "tests I wrote pass".
The report is `.ai/evidence/latest/report.md`. If you cannot run something, say so; never claim it passed.

## Workflow: PRD -> Code -> Test -> Deploy
| Phase | What you do | Where the procedure lives |
|---|---|---|
| PRD | Write acceptance criteria (`AC-xxx`) and the checks that prove them | `.ai/skills/write-prd/`, `.ai/rules/prd.md` |
| Contract | Define the API before code | `.ai/skills/define-contract/`, `.ai/rules/contract.md` |
| Code | Small vertical slices, test first | `.ai/skills/implement-feature/`, `.ai/rules/*` |
| Test | Run the loop until green | `.ai/skills/verify-loop/`, `.ai/skills/fix-failing-gate/` |
| Deploy | Tag, let CD promote, verify the live URL | `.ai/skills/release-and-deploy/` |

Start a feature in one of two ways, then run `./scripts/sdlc implement FEAT-xxx` (the agent writes tests, code, dependencies and config from the spec, and the loop verifies it):
- **From a document:** `./scripts/sdlc spec requirements.pdf` (also .docx, .md, .txt). An agent drafts `prd.md` and `acceptance.json`, the tool validates them, and **you review the draft** before implementing (skill `.ai/skills/review-spec`).
- **By hand:** `./scripts/sdlc new <slug>` creates `.ai/specs/FEAT-xxx-<slug>/`; you write `prd.md` and `acceptance.json`.
Worked example: `.ai/specs/FEAT-000-hello-world/`.

## Commands
```bash
./scripts/sdlc setup      # install dependencies
./scripts/sdlc doctor     # check the toolchain
./scripts/sdlc gates      # lint, types, unit tests, build, contract, security
./scripts/sdlc facts      # PRD acceptance criteria vs the RUNNING system (<%runtimeMode%> runtime)
./scripts/sdlc verify     # gates + facts: exactly what CI runs
./scripts/sdlc loop       # verify -> heal -> verify (max <%maxIterations%> iterations)
./scripts/sdlc spec requirements.pdf   # an agent drafts prd.md + acceptance.json from a document; you review the draft
./scripts/sdlc implement FEAT-001   # spec in (prd.md + acceptance.json), verified code out; needs an agent
./scripts/sdlc sync       # install dependencies if a manifest (pyproject.toml / package.json) changed
```
Single gate while iterating: `./scripts/sdlc gates --only <id>`. `make help` lists the same commands.
On Windows (PowerShell or cmd) the launcher is `.\scripts\sdlc.cmd`; every command and option is the same. Never edit the launchers (`scripts/sdlc`, `scripts/sdlc.cmd`, `scripts/sdlc.py`).

