## Hard constraints
1. Never edit the machinery that defines "correct": `.ai/sdlc.json`, `scripts/sdlc*`, `.github/workflows/`. While healing, also never edit `.ai/specs/`. The loop detects this and stops (exit 4).
2. Never delete, skip or weaken a test or a threshold to get green. Fix the code.
3. Never change `.ai/contract/openapi.json` to hide drift. It changes only when the PRD changes the API.
4. No secrets in the repo (`./scripts/sdlc secrets` enforces it). Config comes from environment variables; see `.env.example`.
5. One feature per branch/PR; reference the `FEAT-xxx` id. Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
6. If the spec is ambiguous or seems wrong, stop and ask. Do not guess requirements.

## When verification fails
Read `.ai/skills/fix-failing-gate/SKILL.md`. In short: reproduce, find the root cause, smallest fix in code, re-run the gate, then the full `verify`.
The loop stops on its own after `<%noProgressLimit%>` identical failures in a row (exit 3) or `<%maxIterations%>` iterations (exit 1): a human looks at it then.

## Agent integration
`./scripts/sdlc implement` and the healing loop run an agent: `.ai/sdlc.json` -> `agent.command`, a shell command that reads the prompt on stdin<%#agentConfigured%> (preset `<%agentPreset%>`, currently `<%agentCommand%>`)<%/agentConfigured%><%^agentConfigured%> (currently empty: the tool prints the prompt and waits for you)<%/agentConfigured%>.
A person picks the agent for their machine with `./scripts/sdlc agent` (saved in `.ai/agent.local.json`, not committed); per run: `./scripts/sdlc implement FEAT-001 --agent <name>` or `SDLC_AGENT_CMD='<your-agent-cli>'`. Do not edit `.ai/sdlc.json` or `.ai/agent.local.json` yourself. Prompts: `.ai/prompts/` (`implement.md` is filled with the feature's prd.md and acceptance.json).
If you are the agent: after adding a dependency to a manifest run `./scripts/sdlc sync`; never edit the spec; never commit or push; if the spec is unclear, write your questions to the file named in the prompt and stop.
Skills are plain Markdown in `.ai/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (frontmatter: name, description). To expose them to a tool that expects another folder, symlink it, e.g. `ln -s ../.ai/skills .claude/skills`.
